{
  "_comment": [
    "The pedagogical gate's rung check (D0 item 3; test_measured_demands.TestTheRungTheItemSitsOn): for every",
    "generated item a rung lists, the demands the app's detectors measured on it that the rung has not taught,",
    "on each rung listing it that no other rung listing it comes before on that rung's path (demands.json's",
    "taughtAt against the rung's ancestry, claims.rung_ancestry, since E0a; since E0b taughtAt is every rung",
    "that teaches the demand, one per path, and a demand is taught where any of them is on the rung's path;",
    "[] is taught nowhere). D0 changes no placement (G18: the round-robin stays), so these are recorded",
    "rather than fixed: the report E's needs-versus-taught gate acts on. The test fails when a combination",
    "appears or goes. Grouped family by rung by demand, with the number of items. Written by D0 from the",
    "plan after its changes; rewritten by E0a when the file's order stopped being read as the path, and by",
    "E0b when taughtAt became a list (the same functions as the build's rung-claims report), and by F2 when options left rungs whose paths had not taught what they carry, and by F2a when 1.5 and 3.1 came to introduce the leap and the note outside the key (2.1 and 3.3 teach them) and each practice rung came to stand on the one before, and by F2b when practice.1 came to stand on 1.1 (the steps on the practice rungs, which 1.1 teaches, off the record)."
  ],
